{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "d2214041-69ee-42ab-8b2a-d08000f1c1aa",
    "name": "Interview Platform — Phase 1 / S3 (Auth Spine)",
    "description": "Proves the auth spine of Phase 1: public health path, Keycloak password-grant login (token stored in a variable), and the protected endpoint through the gateway returning 401 without a token and 200 with it, with issuer and organization_id claim assertions.\n\nFILL ONLY THESE (secrets, Collection -> Variables tab):\n- recruiterAUsername / recruiterAPassword — org A recruiter. Username in the export is 'recruiter1'.\n- recruiterBUsername / recruiterBPassword — org B recruiter. Username in the export is 'recruiter2'.\n\nEverything else is concrete, read from keycloak/realm-export.json and MeController.java:\n- orgAId = 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111\n- orgBId = 22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222\n- /api/me returns keys 'subject' and 'organizationId'\n- interview-web has directAccessGrantsEnabled=true (password grant works)\n- issuer is http://localhost:8180/realms/interview-platform in all three places\n\nDo NOT paste an access token by hand: the Auth requests set {{accessToken}} / {{accessTokenB}} in their test scripts.\n\nRun order (top to bottom, one click): Health -> Auth (sets tokens) -> Protected endpoint.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "_exporter_id": "46902495",
    "_collection_link": "https://go.postman.co/collection/46902495-d2214041-69ee-42ab-8b2a-d08000f1c1aa?source=collection_link"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "1 — Health (public path)",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "GET /actuator/health (public)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "var json;",
                  "pm.test('Response is JSON', function () {",
                  "    json = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(json).to.be.an('object');",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test(\"body.status equals 'UP'\", function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(json.status).to.eql('UP');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{gatewayUrl}}/actuator/health",
              "host": [
                "{{gatewayUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "actuator",
                "health"
              ]
            },
            "description": "The single public path. Must succeed with NO Authorization header."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "2 — Auth (Keycloak)",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "POST token — recruiter A (org A)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "var json = pm.response.json();",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('access_token is present', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(json.access_token, 'no access_token in response').to.be.a('string').and.to.have.length.above(0);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('accessToken', json.access_token);",
                  "",
                  "function decodeJwtPayload(token) {",
                  "    var seg = token.split('.')[1].replace(/-/g, '+').replace(/_/g, '/');",
                  "    while (seg.length % 4) { seg += '='; }",
                  "    var txt = CryptoJS.enc.Utf8.stringify(CryptoJS.enc.Base64.parse(seg));",
                  "    return JSON.parse(txt);",
                  "}",
                  "",
                  "var payload = decodeJwtPayload(json.access_token);",
                  "var expectedIss = pm.collectionVariables.get('keycloakUrl') + '/realms/' + pm.collectionVariables.get('realm');",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('iss equals ' + expectedIss, function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(payload.iss).to.eql(expectedIss);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('organization_id claim is present', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(payload.organization_id, 'organization_id claim missing — check the client protocol mapper').to.exist;",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('organization_id equals org A UUID', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(payload.organization_id).to.eql(pm.collectionVariables.get('orgAId'));",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/x-www-form-urlencoded"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "urlencoded",
              "urlencoded": [
                {
                  "key": "grant_type",
                  "value": "password",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "key": "client_id",
                  "value": "{{clientId}}",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "key": "username",
                  "value": "{{recruiterAUsername}}",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "key": "password",
                  "value": "{{recruiterAPassword}}",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{keycloakUrl}}/realms/{{realm}}/protocol/openid-connect/token",
              "host": [
                "{{keycloakUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "realms",
                "{{realm}}",
                "protocol",
                "openid-connect",
                "token"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Password grant on the public client interview-web. Stores {{accessToken}} and asserts issuer + org A tenant claim."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "POST token — recruiter B (org B)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "var json = pm.response.json();",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('access_token is present', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(json.access_token, 'no access_token in response').to.be.a('string').and.to.have.length.above(0);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('accessTokenB', json.access_token);",
                  "",
                  "function decodeJwtPayload(token) {",
                  "    var seg = token.split('.')[1].replace(/-/g, '+').replace(/_/g, '/');",
                  "    while (seg.length % 4) { seg += '='; }",
                  "    var txt = CryptoJS.enc.Utf8.stringify(CryptoJS.enc.Base64.parse(seg));",
                  "    return JSON.parse(txt);",
                  "}",
                  "",
                  "var payload = decodeJwtPayload(json.access_token);",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('organization_id equals org B UUID', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(payload.organization_id).to.eql(pm.collectionVariables.get('orgBId'));",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('org A and org B carry different organization_id', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.collectionVariables.get('orgAId')).to.not.eql(pm.collectionVariables.get('orgBId'));",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/x-www-form-urlencoded"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "urlencoded",
              "urlencoded": [
                {
                  "key": "grant_type",
                  "value": "password",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "key": "client_id",
                  "value": "{{clientId}}",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "key": "username",
                  "value": "{{recruiterBUsername}}",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "key": "password",
                  "value": "{{recruiterBPassword}}",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{keycloakUrl}}/realms/{{realm}}/protocol/openid-connect/token",
              "host": [
                "{{keycloakUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "realms",
                "{{realm}}",
                "protocol",
                "openid-connect",
                "token"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Proves the two tenants are distinct at the token layer. Stores {{accessTokenB}}. Does NOT call any domain endpoint — none exists yet."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "3 — Protected endpoint through the gateway",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "GET /api/me WITHOUT token (expect 401)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 401', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(401);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{gatewayUrl}}/api/me",
              "host": [
                "{{gatewayUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "me"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Mandatory failure case for this slice: no Authorization header must be rejected by the gateway. Independent of {{accessToken}} — runs cleanly regardless."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /api/me WITH token (expect 200)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "var json;",
                  "pm.test('Response is JSON', function () {",
                  "    json = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(json).to.be.an('object');",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('body.subject is present', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(json.subject).to.be.a('string').and.to.have.length.above(0);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('body.organizationId equals org A UUID', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(json.organizationId).to.eql(pm.collectionVariables.get('orgAId'));",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{accessToken}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{gatewayUrl}}/api/me",
              "host": [
                "{{gatewayUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "me"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Proves the JWT survives the gateway and reaches interview-service, and the tenant claim is exposed as organizationId matching recruiter A's token."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    }
